{#- Parity certificate issued by the rebuild agent when a Python rebuild reproduces the legacy scores. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Parity certificate - {{ model.name }}</title>
<style>
body{font-family:-apple-system,Segoe UI,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:900px;margin:28px auto;padding:0 22px;color:#1d2433;line-height:1.45}
h1{font-size:1.55em;margin-bottom:4px}h2{font-size:1.15em;margin-top:1.7em;border-bottom:1px solid #d5dae3;padding-bottom:4px}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:10px 0}th,td{border:1px solid #d5dae3;padding:6px 9px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}
th{background:#eef1f6;width:38%}.muted{color:#5b6475;font-size:.9em}
.badge{display:inline-block;padding:3px 12px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:600;background:#d7f2df;color:#135c2b}
.num{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}code{font-size:.9em}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Parity certificate</h1>
<p class="muted">{{ model.name }} ({{ model.model_id }}) &middot; rebuild {{ rebuild.rebuild_id }} &middot; issued {{ issued_at }}</p>
<p><span class="badge">PARITY PASSED</span></p>
<p>The Python rebuild reproduces the legacy {{ source_language }} model's score for every record of the legacy
sample within the tolerance below. The comparison was executed in the sandbox by the <code>run_parity</code> tool;
the figures are copied from its result.</p>

<h2>Result</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Records compared</th><td class="num">{{ parity.n_records }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Records outside tolerance</th><td class="num">{{ parity.n_mismatches }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Largest absolute difference</th><td class="num">{{ max_abs_diff }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Tolerance (absolute, per record)</th><td class="num">{{ tolerance }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Attempts needed</th><td class="num">{{ rebuild.attempt }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Code written by</th><td>{{ generator_label }}</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What was compared</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Legacy model</th><td>{{ manifest.get("name", model.name) }}{% if manifest.get("algorithm") %} &middot; {{ manifest["algorithm"] }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Legacy score</th><td><code>{{ score_column }}</code> of the legacy export (fixture <code>{{ fixture_id }}</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Link function</th><td>{{ link }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Terms</th><td>{{ spec.n_numeric_terms }} numeric, {{ spec.n_categorical_terms }} categorical levels{% if spec.categorical_columns %} ({{ spec.categorical_columns | join(", ") }}; reference coding){% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Rebuilt code</th><td><code>{{ rebuild.code.filename }}</code> &middot; SHA-256 <code>{{ rebuild.code.sha256 }}</code></td></tr>
</table>

{% if notes %}
<h2>Design notes</h2>
<ul>{% for n in notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}

<h2>Scope and limits</h2>
<ul>
<li>Parity is proven on the legacy sample only; behaviour on values outside that sample (new category levels,
missing values) is covered by the data-quality gate before every run, not by this certificate.</li>
<li>The certificate is bound to the code hash above: any change to the code requires a new parity run.</li>
<li>Independent sign-off (gate H2) is still required before the rebuilt model is deployed.</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
